{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1529606-lore-of-the-traditions-ch-6-masters-of-what","id":1529606,"title":"Lore of the Traditions Ch 6 : Masters of what ?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-01-28T14:36:42-08:00","id":1529606,"title":"Lore of the Traditions Ch 6 : Masters of what ?","content":"Hi everyone,<br /> <br /> I noticed that the two new hermetic masters in that book, Master Iyeoka Sophia bani Shaea &amp; Master Zagadka Vandamal bani Criamon, don't in fact have a sphere at 5. I tried looking this issue up but couldn't find anything. <br /> <br /> Is this an oversight ? or was it addressed already ? or did the Order decide to grant the title to anyone who trained an apprentice Jedi-style ?<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26426-trianoma4evah","name":"Trianoma4Evah","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-16T06:16:01-08:00","id":1530973,"title":"","content":"I am certain it is an error. The title of magister scolae is awarded only to those who among others requirements have a sphere ranked 5. I really hope this was not a change","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-16T16:17:29-08:00","id":1531009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1529606-lore-of-the-traditions-ch-6-masters-of-what?p=1530973#post1530973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am certain it is an error. The title of magister scolae is awarded only to those who among others requirements have a sphere ranked 5. I really hope this was not a change</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, this book was all over the place with the stat blocks. For exemple infamous temptress Jodi Blake hilariously has neither seduction nor carousing, and Lee Ann Milner has seemingly earned more xp in her 40ish years of life than Porthos in centuries ? <br /> <br /> But like you said : the Order had very precise criteria for recognition and advancement, so if you call yourself a master, you need to meet the requirements <i>and</i> have passed the exam <i>and</i> then have gone through the initiation. A Hermetic who doesn't is very likely to end up in front of someone from House Quaesitor trying to explain that he wasn't committing academic fraud or faking his credentials. <br /> <br /> I just wondered if this had been addressed elsewhere since it apparently wasn't errataed.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26426-trianoma4evah","name":"Trianoma4Evah","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-19T06:08:08-08:00","id":1531107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trianoma4Evah</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1529606-lore-of-the-traditions-ch-6-masters-of-what?p=1531009#post1531009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To be fair, this book was all over the place with the stat blocks. For exemple infamous temptress Jodi Blake hilariously has neither seduction nor carousing, and Lee Ann Milner has seemingly earned more xp in her 40ish years of life than Porthos in centuries ?<br /> <br /> But like you said : the Order had very precise criteria for recognition and advancement, so if you call yourself a master, you need to meet the requirements <i>and</i> have passed the exam <i>and</i> then have gone through the initiation. A Hermetic who doesn't is very likely to end up in front of someone from House Quaesitor trying to explain that he wasn't committing academic fraud or faking his credentials.<br /> <br /> I just wondered if this had been addressed elsewhere since it apparently wasn't errataed.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I thought I was a madman for thinking wtf when I first saw Lee Ann on cult of Ecstacy revised. Either the writer wanted her to have some hyper-specific spells from each sphere and was screwed by the sphere system, or, as someone once told me, she was probably exported of someone's table.. <br /> <br /> But Jodie Blake is more understandable. Every now and then some writer will insist that 300 is a far more reasonable number of abilities than 30, but nobody bothers to remember once the forces of sanity catch up. Unfortunately this time it happened with a core Rulebook <br /> <br /> Anyway, yes, whoever wrote this chapter either forgot made an error or something.. <br /> \u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}